"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2824,"###
 Narrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi, who said: Narrated to us Hushaym, who said: I was informed by Abd al-Malik, who said: I was informed by Ata', who said: Usama ibn Zayd (RA) said: ""I was riding behind the Prophet (ﷺ) at Arafah. He raised both his hands in supplication, and his camel swayed, causing its halter to slip. He caught the halter with one hand while keeping the"
2825,"Narrated to us Yusuf ibn Musa, narrated to us Jarir, on the authority of 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, on the authority of 'Ata', on the authority of Ibn 'Abbas (RA), who said:

""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made the departure (ifadah) from 'Arafat, with Usamah ibn Zayd (RA) riding behind him. He (ﷺ) would raise his hands in supplication such that they did not go beyond his head until he reached al-Jam'. Then he (ﷺ) made the departure from al-Jam', with al-Fadl ibn 'Abbas (RA) riding behind him. Al-Fadl said: 'He (ﷺ) continued to recite the talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah al-'Aqabah.'""

**CHAPTER:**"
